<section class="oil-comparison">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="section-title">Conventional vs. Synthetic Oil</h2>
        
        <div class="comparison-grid">
            
            <div class="comparison-card">
                <h3>Conventional Oil</h3>
                <p>
                    Refined from crude petroleum. Contains natural impurities and breaks down faster under heat and stress. 
                    Suitable for most vehicles with normal driving patterns.
                </p>
                
                <h4>Pros:</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Lower upfront cost per change</li>
                    <li>Readily available everywhere</li>
                    <li>Adequate for normal driving conditions</li>
                    <li>Works well in older engines</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h4>Cons:</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Breaks down faster in heat</li>
                    <li>Requires more frequent changes (3,000-5,000 miles)</li>
                    <li>Less protection in extreme conditions</li>
                    <li>Contains more impurities</li>
                </ul>
                
                <div class="best-for">
                    Best For: Budget-conscious drivers, older vehicles, normal driving conditions
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="comparison-card">
                <h3>Synthetic Oil</h3>
                <p>
                    Engineered at the molecular level for superior performance. Resists breakdown, flows better in cold 
                    weather, and protects better in extreme heat. Costs more but lasts longer.
                </p>
                
                <h4>Pros:</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Superior engine protection</li>
                    <li>Longer change intervals (7,000-10,000 miles)</li>
                    <li>Better performance in extreme temperatures</li>
                    <li>Cleaner engine operation</li>
                    <li>Improved fuel economy</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h4>Cons:</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Higher cost per oil change</li>
                    <li>May not be necessary for all vehicles</li>
                </ul>
                
                <div class="best-for">
                    Best For: Newer vehicles, high-performance engines, extreme driving conditions, maximum protection
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</section>

